# What `docker build -f services/auth/Dockerfile .` may NOT see.
#
# The build context is the repo root (auth needs libs/go), so this
# file lists paths from the repo root. Docker picks it up automatically
# because it is named <Dockerfile name>.dockerignore and sits next to
# the Dockerfile — each service can have its own.
#
# Approach: ignore EVERYTHING, then allow the two folders the build
# needs. A new folder in the repo can never leak into the image by
# accident.
*
!libs/go
!services/auth

# …and inside those two folders, still leave out:

# Secrets — never send these to the build context
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Docker files themselves (changing them shouldn't bust the COPY cache)
**/Dockerfile
**/*.dockerignore

# Build output
**/bin/
**/dist/

# Development tools
**/Makefile

# Go test files — not needed in production image
**/*_test.go

# Docs
**/*.md

# OS / IDE
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
